## Context

IDH's `ticket-new` skill creates `.erg` files via direct Write tool calls.
This hits the Claude Code permission layer. A binary command makes creation
atomic and permission-free.

## Actions

Implement `erg new <title> [dir]`:
- Call `erg next-id` internally to get the next ID
- Prompt or accept `--author`, `--created` flags (default: current user, today)
- Write a minimal valid v1 ticket with Title, Created, Author, log separator,
  body separator
- Output: the new filename (e.g., `0042-my-title.erg`)

Slug generation: lowercase the title, replace spaces/special chars with `-`,
truncate to 40 chars.

## Exit criteria

- `erg new "Add branch-as-claim to erg ready"` creates `NNNN-add-branch-as-claim-to-erg-ready.erg`
- File passes `erg validate`
- ID is the correct next sequential ID
- Test: create in temp dir, validate, check filename and content
